<title>PAKISTAN: Karachi port handles 83,226 tonnes cargo.</title>
<headline>Karachi port handles 83,226 tonnes cargo.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1997-02-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistan's Karachi Port Trust said it had handled 83,226 tonnes of export and import cargo in the 24 hours to 7 a.m. (0200 GMT) on Wednesday compared to 71,191 tonnes in the same period on Tuesday.</p>
<p>Cargo handling in tonnes:</p>
<p>				    Wednesday   Feb 18</p>
<p>    Export cargo		22,715	24,262</p>
<p>    Import cargo		60,511	46,929</p>
<p>In the past 24 hours, three ships sailed and six berthed. In the next 24 hours, seven are expected to sail and 13 are expected to arrive.  </p>
<p>Berthing schedule of major vessels unloading or expected to unload at Karachi Port:</p>
<p>    Commodity	  Tonnes/TEUs  Ship		   Berthing</p>
<p>Crude oil		70,000	 Stavros - I	 19/2</p>
<p>Chemicals		 2,293	 NCC Jouf	    21/2</p>
<p>Fertiliser	     24,602	 Athinoula	   23/2</p>
<p>Containers		  650	 Fen He		20/2</p>
<p>-- Karachi newsroom 9221-5685192</p>
